From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Kane <jkane@tds.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:40:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [VectraOS] FoundationEssentials for the *-vectraos triples

Essentials only (SWIFTFOUNDATION_ESSENTIALS_ONLY, after swift-on-vectra's
switch: no ICU, nothing fetched), with VectraOS's C library through its
platform module, VectraOSLibc, and files through its POSIX calls (fdio
over VectraOS's fs service):

- Each C library import gains a VectraOSLibc branch; TARGET_OS_VECTRAOS.
- Where WASI lacks what VectraOS lacks too, VectraOS joins its gates: no
  users or groups, no extended attributes, no file system attributes
  (statvfs), no sendfile, no fchown, no sticky bit, the current time zone
  GMT until a time service; NO_C_LOCALE, NO_LOCALIZATION and NO_TZFILE
  are the build's (one locale, no zone files yet).
- No mmap yet: files are read; times aren't set (the fs service keeps
  them): setAttributes with a modification date is featureUnsupported,
  and a copy keeps the new node's.
- uuid.c: randomness from getentropy (croi's CPRNG), the monotonic clock,
  and a UUID's string parsed directly (no sscanf yet); _CStdlib.h skips
  <tgmath.h>, which needs <complex.h>.
- Date.description computes the civil date itself (no gmtime_r or
  strftime yet).
